WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.990
Meet Xiao Zhu, a fictional patient, collecting a repeat prescription.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.050
In the story, the pharmacy's screen opens his whole record for one medicine.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:19.070
With MedSSI, the pharmacy sees only what the pickup needs: the medicine and dose, the days' supply, an allergy check.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:29.324
MedSSI's 2025 story pages, re-run on a laptop in 2026: first the problem, then the fix.

00:00:29.324 --> 00:00:31.620
Both are scripted pages.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:39.980
MedSSI's idea: the hospital issues a digital credential once, into the government wallet app on his phone.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:45.780
Issuing and signature checks ran on the Ministry of Digital Affairs' test sandbox.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:58.577
In the team's 2025 recording, the sandbox answers both sides: a one-time QR to issue an allergy card, and, in a separate run, a request QR for a consent check.

00:00:58.577 --> 00:01:00.710
The phone scan wasn't filmed.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:07.550
How it works: the pharmacy asks only for the pickup fields; his wallet shows what will be shared.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.952
He agrees, and only those go.

00:01:09.952 --> 00:01:14.340
MedSSI's server check rejects any field that wasn't requested.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.745
Share the prescription, not the record.

00:01:20.745 --> 00:01:26.480
MedSSI was a 2025 student prototype on a test sandbox, not a medical product.
